<article class="about-page">
  <h1>About this notebook</h1>

  <p class="lede">I keep this page the way one keeps a lab notebook:
  dated, cross-referenced, and honest about what failed.</p>

  <h2>What lives here</h2>
  <p>Long-form notes on systems programming, typography, and small tools.
  Short discoveries go straight into dated entries; anything that survives
  three rereads gets promoted to an essay.</p>

  <h2>Colophon</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Type:</strong> Lora for body, Merriweather for titles,
        Ubuntu Mono for code.</li>
    <li><strong>Content:</strong> one shared Markdown collection powers both
        this blue notebook and the dithered-ink edition.</li>
    <li><strong>Build:</strong> Eleventy turns Markdown into static HTML;
        GitHub Pages serves the result without a client-side framework.</li>
    <li><strong>Interaction:</strong> page cross-fades, heading anchors,
        footnote pairing, code copy buttons, a footer clock, and reduced-motion
        support remain progressive enhancements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Add only the contact channels you want to maintain publicly.</p>
</article>
